WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.437
The federal requirement.

2
00:00:01.437 --> 00:00:06.717
The guide's Gate 5 table maps actuation
to NIST special publication eight hundred

3
00:00:06.717 --> 00:00:11.997
fifty-three: access restrictions for
change, access enforcement, least privilege,

4
00:00:11.997 --> 00:00:17.276
change control, session audit and the plan
of action and milestones, and to special

5
00:00:17.276 --> 00:00:22.400
publication eight hundred sixty-three B,
revision four, for resets and recovery.

6
00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:25.595
The Gate 6 table maps the
re-read to change control,

7
00:00:25.595 --> 00:00:30.738
verification of controls, continuous
monitoring and audit record generation.

8
00:00:30.738 --> 00:00:33.450
Chapter 05 adds separation of duties:

9
00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:37.038
no person can close a
finding by setting its state.

10
00:00:37.038 --> 00:00:42.751
The evidence an ISSO keeps: connector and
spoke identities with their permissions,

11
00:00:42.751 --> 00:00:47.636
provisioning events, activation
records and change records for Gate 5;

12
00:00:47.636 --> 00:00:52.355
and for Gate 6, the evidence attachment
and hash on each closed record,

13
00:00:52.355 --> 00:00:56.826
the re-read result and time, and
the verifier account's audit trail.

14
00:00:56.826 --> 00:01:00.580
Before shipping, work through
the Chapter 05 checklist.
